                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5294: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chairman of the American Delegation to the Sixth International
                        Conference of American States</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hughes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-23T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. For Mr. Francis White. The following is the text of the substitute project
                    approved by the Chamber of Deputies as telegraphed by Munro:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text quoted in paragraph 2 of telegram No. 36, January 20, 9
                    a.m., from the Chargé in Nicaragua, printed on <ref target="#pg440">page
                        440</ref>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
